turning and he's coming.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:26.930
(crowd cheering)

00:06:28.752 --> 00:06:30.253
This could be it!

00:06:30.253 --> 00:06:31.683
(crowd cheering)

00:06:31.683 --> 00:06:33.851
Conor McGregor is victorious.

00:06:33.851 --> 00:06:36.268
The crowd go absolutely wild.

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:41.423
He gets in what training
that he was looking for.

00:06:43.111 --> 00:06:45.139
- [Interviewer] Did you
ever have, let's call it

00:06:45.139 --> 00:06:47.608
a normal job, Conor? A 9 to 5?

00:06:47.608 --> 00:06:51.065
- Yeah because the Irish
thing is to getting to trade

00:06:51.065 --> 00:06:51.898
straightaway.

00:06:51.898 --> 00:06:52.731
I was no different.

00:06:52.731 --> 00:06:55.208
As soon as I finished school

00:06:55.208 --> 00:06:56.210
I was always getting pestered.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:57.152
What are you doing with your life?

00:06:57.152 --> 00:06:57.985
You know?

00:06:57.985 --> 00:06:59.767
Doing this, doing that.

00:06:59.767 --> 00:07:01.120
They didn't know what it was.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.689
They didn't know MMA was,
they didn't know none of this.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:04.894
They didn't know I could
make a career out of it.

00:07:04.894 --> 00:07:05.770
As far as they were concerned,

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.043
mom and dad I'm talking about, I was just

00:07:07.043 --> 00:07:09.797
getting into a cage and
fighting with some other guy.

00:07:09.797 --> 00:07:10.807
They didn't know nothing about it.

00:07:10.807 --> 00:07:13.161
No one did, really, but I knew.

00:07:13.161 --> 00:07:14.335
You know what I mean?

00:07:14.335 --> 00:07:16.935
I knew and then I ended up getting a trade

00:07:16.935 --> 00:07:18.568
just to keep them quiet
because I used to have

00:07:18.568 --> 00:07:19.943
a lot of fights with me dad. A lot

00:07:19.943 --> 00:07:20.848
- [Interviewer] What trade did you get?

00:07:20.848 --> 00:07:23.335
- I ended up getting a trade as a plumber.

00:07:23.335 --> 00:07:27.418
Literally opened the back
alleys on the Wicklow Mountains.

00:07:27.418 --> 00:07:29.350
I feel that site was one of the biggest

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:31.997
sites in Europe, Kiltearn.

00:07:31.997 --> 00:07:34.561
It was right at that skiing place, huge.

00:07:34.561 --> 00:07:35.763
And now it's just abandoned.

00:07:35.763 --> 00:07:36.840
Now it's just deserted.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:38.083
So, I used to go up there six o'clock,

00:07:38.083 --> 00:07:39.951
five o'clock in the
morning I was on my M-50.

00:07:39.951 --> 00:07:41.847
I used to have to walk to the N-4,

00:07:41.847 --> 00:07:43.533
about half an hour from me.

00:07:43.533 --> 00:07:44.784
Hellish, waiting for some limited guy

00:07:44.784 --> 00:07:45.617
that I didn't even know.

00:07:45.617 --> 00:07:46.549
He drove on the N-4 and I'd have

00:07:46.549 --> 00:07:48.092
to flag him down.

00:07:48.092 --> 00:07:48.925
Nightmare, yeah.

00:07:48.925 --> 00:07:51.000
Two hours down on the
M-50, two hours back.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.084
Usually 14 hour days and
I was the first year.

00:07:53.084 --> 00:07:55.274
So, I had to go and do everything.

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:56.148
I had to go to the shop.

00:07:56.148 --> 00:07:58.037
I had to go and get this and get that.

00:07:58.037 --> 00:07:59.228
So, I always had trouble with that.

00:07:59.228 --> 00:08:00.515
I was like, this isn't for me.

00:08:00.515 --> 00:08:01.461
This is not for me.

00:08:01.461 --> 00:08:03.026
- [Interviewer] How long did you last?

00:08:03.026 --> 00:08:05.864
- I lasted 18 months doing
it, but it was tough.

00:08:05.864 --> 00:08:08.031
It wasn't the life for me.

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:11.319
And then John said, because
I was training with John

00:08:11.319 --> 00:08:12.530
as well at the time.

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:15.336
And then John got in touch
and says, "I have a show.

00:08:15.336 --> 00:08:16.688
On the show would you
like to fight on it?"

00:08:16.688 --> 00:08:17.806
And that was it.

00:08:17.806 --> 00:08:19.207
I just packed it in, didn't show up.

00:08:19.207 --> 00:08:21.137
Me dad used to come in
and punch the hell out me

00:08:21.137 --> 00:08:24.047
and try to drag me out of
bed and I just wouldn't go.

00:08:24.047 --> 00:08:25.424
And I remember I hadn't
up law for a good few

00:08:25.424 --> 00:08:28.091
years removable and that was it.

00:08:29.572 --> 00:08:31.923
I just packed it in, quit,
and then focused on training.

00:08:31.923 --> 00:08:34.308
I knew what was going to happen.

00:08:34.308 --> 00:08:36.042
I knew I was going to
get here, they didn't.

00:08:36.042 --> 00:08:38.598
It was a lot of stressful
years, you know what I mean?

00:08:38.598 --> 00:08:42.585
A lot of tough times,
but I proved them wrong.

00:08:42.585 --> 00:08:43.728
I proved myself right.

00:08:43.728 --> 00:08:46.311
(upbeat music)

00:08:48.254 --> 00:08:50.193
- [Commentator] Conor McGregor.

00:08:50.193 --> 00:08:52.749
- [Commentator] Oh, see Steve O'Keefe.

00:08:52.749 --> 00:08:54.265
(crowd cheering)

00:08:54.265 --> 00:08:55.236
Need to defend.

00:08:55.236 --> 00:08:57.545
Again, the inside elbow's coming in.

00:08:57.545 --> 00:08:59.154
- [Commentator] This evening.

00:08:59.154 --> 00:09:02.334
Oh, wow, righteously, Steve O'Keefe was

00:09:02.334 --> 00:09:04.310
- [Commentator] He was out.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.993
- [Commentator] He was
unconscious from those strikes.

00:09:06.993 --> 00:09:08.179
- [Commentator] He's just come back round

00:09:08.179 --> 00:09:10.012
and Conor McGregor is.

00:09:11.001 --> 00:09:13.590
- Every gym I went to was always,

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:15.067
they had their set way.

00:09:15.067 --> 00:09:17.857
Every gym had their set
way of doing things.

00:09:17.857 --> 00:09:20.810
Don't do it this way, do it that way.

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:22.654
So, that was just a normal
thing that I thought.

00:09:22.654 --> 00:09:25.140
I thought people just
had their own set way

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:26.856
and you must do it that way.

00:09:26.856 --> 00:09:28.086
You must stand this way.

00:09:28.086 --> 00:09:29.157
You must kick this way.

00:09:29.157 --> 00:09:30.124
You must punch this way.

00:09:30.124 --> 00:09:31.928
But with John, when I went to John,

00:09:31.928 --> 00:09:34.148
I met my coach, John Kavanagh,

00:09:34.148 --> 00:09:35.641
at Straight Blast Gym it wasn't like that.

00:09:35.641 --> 00:09:39.296
He had a more open mind and he encouraged

00:09:39.296 --> 00:09:42.037
different movements and
I'd never experienced

00:09:42.037 --> 00:09:42.870
that before.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:45.507
I'd never heard a coach
say that to me before.

00:09:45.507 --> 00:09:46.794
And that stuck in my
head and I talked to him.

00:09:46.794 --> 00:09:51.358
And I said, "This guy is
thinking outside the box."

00:09:51.358 --> 00:09:53.589
He has a vision that everything works

00:09:53.589 --> 00:09:56.859
and he encourages every
movement because ultimately

00:09:56.859 --> 00:09:59.626
there is a time and a place
for every single move.

00:09:59.626 --> 00:10:02.209
So, I just knew when I met John

00:10:03.293 --> 00:10:05.039
and when he spoke it made

00:10:05.039 --> 00:10:06.488
complete sense to me and that was it.

00:10:06.488 --> 00:10:07.836
I stuck with him and he stuck with me

00:10:07.836 --> 00:10:09.409
and the rest is history.

00:10:09.409 --> 00:10:11.992
(upbeat music)

00:10:13.468 --> 00:10:14.553
- [Commentator] Favorite
striking technique

00:10:14.553 --> 00:10:16.612
and we see the punch that lands.

00:10:16.612 --> 00:10:19.195
(upbeat music)

00:10:25.462 --> 00:10:27.782
- [Commentator] Seconds
away from being stopped.

00:10:27.782 --> 00:10:29.240
- [Commentator] That's it.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:30.073
That's it.

00:10:30.073 --> 00:10:30.906
- [Commentator] It is a whopper!

00:10:30.906 --> 00:10:33.527
Conor McGregor stops Dennis Siver.

00:10:33.527 --> 00:10:34.360
- [Commentator] Look at this.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.193
Look at this.

00:10:35.193 --> 00:10:38.272
He's going up to Jose Aldo.

00:10:38.272 --> 00:10:39.105
Look at this.

00:10:39.105 --> 00:10:40.605
Look at Jose Aldo.

00:10:44.509 --> 00:10:47.553
- Gratitude is one of the most strongest

00:10:47.553 --> 00:10:50.970
forms of power in attracting good things.

00:10:52.717 --> 00:10:55.733
If you truly feel grateful
for the things in your life.

00:10:55.733 --> 00:10:58.470
I always felt grateful
for even the small things.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:00.107
I always used to celebrate
the small things.

00:11:00.107 --> 00:11:02.295
Now I might be celebrating
the bigger things,

00:11:02.295 --> 00:11:04.652
but I always celebrate
every little good thing

00:11:04.652 --> 00:11:06.068
that would happen to me
in my life even before

00:11:06.068 --> 00:11:07.638
I had any kind of money or any of that.

00:11:07.638 --> 00:11:09.879
I would celebrate and I
would feel grateful for it.

00:11:09.879 --> 00:11:13.785
And it just gave me more and
this is exactly the same thing

00:11:13.785 --> 00:11:14.747
that's happening right now.

00:11:14.747 --> 00:11:17.866
I still remain grateful and more comes.

00:11:17.866 --> 00:11:20.449
(upbeat music)

00:11:22.136 --> 00:11:23.980
- [Commentator] Hands at his hips.

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:24.813
(crowd cheering)

00:11:24.813 --> 00:11:27.230
- [Commentator] Working good.

00:11:29.132 --> 00:11:30.132
Just ranked.

00:11:32.173 --> 00:11:34.391
- [Commentator] Wow.

00:11:34.391 --> 00:11:36.032
That's the real deal, ladies

00:11:36.032 --> 00:11:36.865
and gentlemen.

00:11:36.865 --> 00:11:40.531
Make no mistake about it,
Conor McGregor is for real.

00:11:40.531 --> 00:11:42.501
- [Commentator] An entire
country is standing

00:11:42.501 --> 00:11:43.978
on their feet right now.

00:11:43.978 --> 00:11:46.518
- [Commentator] He really
did just make it look easy.

00:11:46.518 --> 00:11:48.236
He said he would make it look easy,

00:11:48.236 --> 00:11:50.311
he made it look easy.

00:11:50.311 --> 00:11:51.441
That's the real deal.

00:11:51.441 --> 00:11:56.274
- [Commentator] He said, "First
round KO," mark my words.

00:11:56.274 --> 00:11:57.819
- [Commentator] We believed him.

00:11:57.819 --> 00:12:00.929
I mean, that was just glorious.

00:12:00.929 --> 00:12:02.737
- Of course I am familiar
with Muhammad Ali.

00:12:02.737 --> 00:12:04.810
You don't just have
him here, he is global.

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:06.698
He is the man.

00:12:06.698 --> 00:12:09.096
Muhammad Ali was a guy
that done what had not

00:12:09.096 --> 00:12:10.645
been done before.

00:12:10.645 --> 00:12:11.478
Change the face,

00:12:11.478 --> 00:12:13.020
not only the face of his game,

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:14.067
but the face of the world.

00:12:14.067 --> 00:12:18.768
He was outspoken, he fought
for what he believed in.

00:12:18.768 --> 00:12:20.966
He was charismatic.

00:12:20.966 --> 00:12:24.966
He was a legend, a hero,
and I looked up to him.

00:12:26.109 --> 00:12:29.167
One of my first heroes was Muhammad Ali.

00:12:29.167 --> 00:12:32.652
When I was 11 years old
there was a group of people

00:12:32.652 --> 00:12:35.772
and they tried to attack
me and a fight broke out

00:12:35.772 --> 00:12:37.712
and it was just me and one guy

00:12:37.712 --> 00:12:40.795
before everyone else jumped in on me,

00:12:42.405 --> 00:12:44.428
but we were fighting each other.

00:12:44.428 --> 00:12:48.534
And I slipped a punch and
I shuffled my shoulders

00:12:48.534 --> 00:12:50.915
and said, "Muhammad
Ali!" And threw a shot.

00:12:50.915 --> 00:12:53.466
And he rolled under the
shot but fell into a knee

00:12:53.466 --> 00:12:54.423
and I ended up on top of him.

00:12:54.423 --> 00:12:56.239
So, I'm out there calling
myself Muhammad Ali

00:12:56.239 --> 00:12:57.225
and I'm punching him in the head.

00:12:57.225 --> 00:12:58.527
Then somebody came in and tried to kick me

00:12:58.527 --> 00:13:00.107
and then a whole group of them came in

00:13:00.107 --> 00:13:02.972
and it was just a big fight, but it was me

00:13:02.972 --> 00:13:03.805
against six of them.

00:13:03.805 --> 00:13:05.559
And I ended up getting my ass whooped.

00:13:05.559 --> 00:13:08.038
- [Interviewer] But that
first guy, you whooped him out

00:13:08.038 --> 00:13:09.155
and you said, "Muhammad Ali".

00:13:09.155 --> 00:13:12.055
- I done the Ali shuffle.

00:13:12.055 --> 00:13:13.444
I'm only 11 years old.

00:13:13.444 --> 00:13:15.786
I done the Ali shuffle, threw a left hook.

00:13:15.786 --> 00:13:17.310
He rolled under the left hook.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:19.169
It was good of him to roll.

00:13:19.169 --> 00:13:20.454
He saw it coming and rolled under it,

00:13:20.454 --> 00:13:21.740
but he rolled right into a knee.

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:22.990
I was prepared.

00:13:24.959 --> 00:13:27.376
I was studying tape, so yeah.

00:13:28.881 --> 00:13:31.017
No, so definitely Muhammad
Ali was a hero of mine.

00:13:31.017 --> 00:13:33.600
(upbeat music)

00:13:35.202 --> 00:13:37.373
- [Commentator] Conor's
12 wins, 11 are knockouts

00:13:37.373 --> 00:13:38.444
- [Commentator] Caught him
with the uppercut there.

00:13:38.444 --> 00:13:40.071
- [Commentator] Are knockouts
and he almost did it again

00:13:40.071 --> 00:13:40.904
- [Commentator] Going backwards.

00:13:40.904 --> 00:13:43.110
- [Commentator] Look at that upper.

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:45.650
(upbeat music)

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:47.237
- [Commentator] Uppercut.

00:13:47.237 --> 00:13:49.820
(upbeat music)

00:13:56.711 --> 00:13:58.965
- [Commentator] Looking to finish it here.

00:13:58.965 --> 00:14:01.801
This is why everyone's been
talking about Conor McGregor.

00:14:01.801 --> 00:14:03.008
- [Commentator] It's all over.

00:14:03.008 --> 00:14:06.758
Connor McGregor another
first round win, wow!

00:14:09.637 --> 00:14:11.887
Ultra impressive UFC debut.

00:14:14.724 --> 00:14:17.343
- [Commentator] That is
exactly why he's so dangerous.

00:14:17.343 --> 00:14:19.048
- I don't like to think too far ahead.

00:14:19.048 --> 00:14:19.881
- [Interviewer] So, you haven't thought

00:14:19.881 --> 00:14:20.714
alternative careers

00:14:20.714 --> 00:14:21.945
- No, I don't like thinking too far ahead.

00:14:21.945 --> 00:14:24.707
People set goals, long
distance goals and shit.

00:14:24.707 --> 00:14:26.067
That's too much for me.

00:14:26.067 --> 00:14:27.607
I already feel like I'm living it

00:14:27.607 --> 00:14:29.018
and then I just carry on.

00:14:29.018 --> 00:14:33.424
I carry on day by day already
living the final goal,

00:14:33.424 --> 00:14:34.738
the goal of being the world champion.

00:14:34.738 --> 00:14:36.604
I already carry myself
like I'm a world champion.

00:14:36.604 --> 00:14:39.917
I already speak like I'm a
world champion and that's it.

00:14:39.917 --> 00:14:42.616
I just carry on day by day
so I'll take it as it comes.

00:14:42.616 --> 00:14:46.904
Again, like I said, you're
asking me about the future.

00:14:46.904 --> 00:14:48.566
I'll let you know a little bit closer,

00:14:48.566 --> 00:14:50.025
you know what I mean?

00:14:50.025 --> 00:14:52.135
All I can see right now is the gold.

00:14:52.135 --> 00:14:53.221
That's all I can see.

00:14:53.221 --> 00:14:55.804
(upbeat music)

00:14:57.737 --> 00:14:59.396
- [Commentator] Outside strikes back.

00:14:59.396 --> 00:15:01.038
- [Commentator] It was
so very well executed.

00:15:01.038 --> 00:15:03.318
Ivan Buchinger having a horribly.

00:15:03.318 --> 00:15:04.172
